# Build + headless run verification (2026-10-25)

## Build
- `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 cargo build -p cnc-launcher -p cnc-map-editor` — Finished
  dev profile in 53.35s, 0 errors. Binaries at RUST/target/debug/{cnc-launcher,
  cnc-map-editor}.

## Launcher (headless)
- `./target/debug/cnc-launcher --frames 3` → exit 0 after ~30s. Log shows the TD
  demo scene simulating (harvester unloads, credits 575→700).
- CLI verified via `--help`: mission/scenario/campaign/replay/net-role/menu
  modes; wgpu default with software fallback.

## Map editor (two entry points)
- `cargo run -p cnc-map-editor --example tileset_render` → exit 0,
  saved /tmp/opencode/tileset_qa.png (2616x1312 RGBA PNG, two-panel tileset QA
  harness: left exact cell size, right +0.5 half-texel, per InRepo pack).
- `./target/debug/cnc-map-editor --headless --screenshot ... --frames 2` → exit
  0, "headless self-test OK", saved /tmp/opencode/editor_headless.png
  (1400x900 RGBA PNG). It also emitted a stray RUST/maps/headless_map.ini
  (72 KB self-test product) which was removed; working tree clean after.

## Notes
- Full GUI run requires a display/wayland session; headless modes above exercise
  the same sim/UI draw paths (the editor example explicitly mirrors
  `tiles::base_draw` + `ui_tile_rect` used by the editor UI).
